{"title":"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(the_best_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (the best solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Area)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Area)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(centroid)_(fastest_way)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (centroid) (fastest way)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallelogram\" title=\"Parallelogram\">parallelogram</a> with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Vertex\" title=\"Vertex\">vertices</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac1e87345d7bebc0db18364cb46efdef829cc71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10,45)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/e/04e0fe463249ac00f8bbd3fec484f7d4dafedeee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10,114)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d63d8a4c8f07d0f6d010eec6c5ecb2820218ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(28,153)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/e/8ee2bab752cb31539850ab29d5ceec3d99d84dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(28,84)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />.  A <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">line</a> through the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Origin\" title=\"Origin\">origin</a> cuts this figure into two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Congruent\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Congruent\">congruent</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">polygons</a>.  The <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Slope\" title=\"Slope\">slope</a> of the line is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/271cdd78c4c10cde94410584ce7282874413cb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d68403b2262cd441edb65005adf53304fdfda5c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{}$\" width=\"15\" height=\"8\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/b/c8b61c20d22f13c0586a382c14a5710b6a4afe1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_{}$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relatively_prime\" title=\"Relatively prime\">relatively prime</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a>.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let the first point on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec186fd1809357d1f530bee2334ceb59d405b4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/e/e8e9a1ec2d960ab81ed1e2a519a81dd4ca05540a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10,45+a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> where a is the height above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac1e87345d7bebc0db18364cb46efdef829cc71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10,45)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />.  Let the second point on the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/6/676c88bbf0f79f4170c0d13df2d3c49f45287ce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=28$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/3/5f3733cd1e33098badead55c55eeab3229c1d78f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(28, 153-a)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />. For two given points, the line will pass the origin if the coordinates are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Proportion\" title=\"Proportion\">proportional</a> (such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/3/103b75c75f08c57c2cbe25930bf1a7249d05cf7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{y_1}{x_1} = \\frac{y_2}{x_2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />). Then, we can write that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/9/ac98ff43b1f4005a016b1068be01f49aecf83780.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45 + a}{10} = \\frac{153 - a}{28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"38\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/c/54c8987ff795d6a0dff33aaf50f52ae555846d27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1530 - 10a = 1260 + 28a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"196\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/f/65f391a335048a385dd204a2371b7dae67c5d811.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\frac{270}{38}=\\frac{135}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"119\" height=\"38\" />. The slope of the line (since it passes through the origin) is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/1/fe1c432ae856b84f82bfac6a3a38c7134fc79e6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{45 + \\frac{135}{19}}{10} = \\frac{99}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"113\" height=\"41\" />, and the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/d/1ad4a6b8954fe74db478370f78b457c58e1e6013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n = \\boxed{118}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28the_best_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(the_best_solution)\">Solution 2 (the best solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (the best solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>You can clearly see that a line that cuts a parallelogram into two congruent pieces must go through the center of the parallelogram. Taking the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0ac1e87345d7bebc0db18364cb46efdef829cc71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10,45)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/d/17d63d8a4c8f07d0f6d010eec6c5ecb2820218ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(28,153)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c47b29eb76e4eddbe5da25ce439f1345fda8e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(19,99)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, which is the center of the parallelogram. Thus the slope of the line must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/b/58bbadd49e022c09c17af112dc8cc88f8aa7826a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{99}{19}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />, and the solution is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c851b8731ef9deac914acfd0c0e569472391ec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{118}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Edit by ngourise: if u dont think this is the best solution then smh\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Area.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Area)\">Solution 3 (Area)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Area)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note that the area of the parallelogram is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/4/874e0b96aa8a1f8740e63174a72011ce95ec83dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69 \\cdot 18 = 1242,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"113\" height=\"16\" /> so the area of each of the two trapezoids with congruent area is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/3/3833ec104c8c5372d6f13f5b276977da71647aef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$621.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> Therefore, since the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/c/cec7bae5d48b5e05ced38cdb2ed6741a0c16f953.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" /> the sum of the bases of each trapezoid must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/1/bf1486ebee8a50705a98ca2056a1dd5582f94154.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$69.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> \n</p><p>The points where the line in question intersects the long side of the parallelogram can be denoted as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/0/690a869ce8ec548f813e3a2cc75ac8f77a150aba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(10, \\frac{10m}{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f495b14715b88fd56190d632e0433b755b10625.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(28, \\frac{28m}{n}),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"82\" height=\"37\" /> respectively. We see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/e/5ce8800a58e07efdc5b8c8dbdaa8542b5aaeab1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10m}{n} - 45 + \\frac{28m}{n} - 84 = 69,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"225\" height=\"37\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/0/210cb85fea4a30734802e48485d7784e23f360be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{38m}{n} = 198 \\implies \\frac{m}{n} = \\frac{99}{19} \\implies \\boxed{118}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"297\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Solution by Ilikeapos\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28centroid.29_.28fastest_way.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(centroid)_(fastest_way)\">Solution 4 (centroid) (fastest way)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (centroid) (fastest way)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/3951fa0c2bb465aac7a3712d8727213e9562bc60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\Sigma x_i /4, \\Sigma y_i /4)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"117\" height=\"20\" /> is the centroid, which generates <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c47b29eb76e4eddbe5da25ce439f1345fda8e18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(19,99)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c851b8731ef9deac914acfd0c0e569472391ec2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{118}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />. This is the fastest way because you do not need to find the opposite vertices by drawing.\n</p><p>Solution by maxamc\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME\" title=\"1999 AIME\">1999 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1999 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1999\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1999_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1999 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016224429\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.047 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.095 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 276/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 6578/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion 